7. Causal Ledger and Normative Audit

7.1 Causal Ledger

Every major state transition has an explanation:

X_{t+1} = F(X_t, a_t, \eta_t).

A causal ledger entry includes the action, primitive sequence, derived deltas, feasibility verdict, authority verdict, and normative evaluations.

7.2 Normative Audit Ledger

Each action is logged with a list of normative evaluations:

\begin{array}{c}
(\text{evaluator}, \text{criterion}, \text{verdict}, \text{weight}).
\end{array}

The simulator does not compute a single desirability scalar D_t. It records who evaluated what, by which criterion, and with what weight.

Any later aggregation into a desirability scalar is a post hoc human or institutional act, not part of the engine.

This preserves

\text{Feasibility} \neq \text{Authority} \neq \text{Desirability}.

---

8. Core Algorithm and Operator-Splitting Order

8.1 Operator-Splitting

The order of subsystem updates within a macro-step changes the propagation speed of cascading failures. The following order is fixed.

1. Integrate all critical buffers with event detection.
2. Process any buffer-failure events immediately.
3. Apply discrete action resource, exergy, waste, knowledge, and authority deltas.
4. Update infrastructure decay and resource depletion.
5. Update population and HANDY-Space using buffer levels from the end of the buffer-integration step.
6. Update authority and legitimacy using population and inequality from the end of the population step.
7. Record causal ledger and normative audit.

This ordering ensures that a buffer failure detected in step 1 propagates to population in the same macro-step, not one macro-step later.

8.2 Minimal Viable Scope

The first implementation remains deliberately small:

· One star.
· Three bodies: Earth, Moon, Mars.
· Five fundamental resources: Water, Oxygen, Carbon, Metals, Exergy.
· Three agent classes: Human, AI, Robot.
· Five infrastructure categories: Habitat, Energy, Agriculture, Industry, Transport.
· Five fundamental state variables: Population, Exergy, Resources, Knowledge, Infrastructure.
· One authority state \Lambda_t with threshold intervals.
· One wealth-buffered HANDY-Space subsystem.
· One hybrid event scheduler.

8.3 Implementation Order

1. Build the physical/resource simulation with simple rule-based agents.
2. Implement the causal ledger and viability metrics Q_t^{\text{short}}, Q_t^{\text{reserve}}.
3. Implement robust feasibility with pessimistic interval bounds.
4. Implement the authority state \Lambda_t with interval thresholds.
5. Implement the human agency index H_t.
6. Run the energy-demand sweep.
7. Run the authority-threshold sweep.
8. Add wealth-buffered HANDY-Space and the extinction floor.
9. Add AI agents with the structured action grammar.
10. Add the full normative audit ledger.

AI agents should not be used in step 1 or step 6. If rule-based agents cannot establish a viable settlement, AI agents will not help.

