Appendix F. Authority Dynamics and Human Agency

F.1 Authority State

Let \Lambda_{i,j}(t)\in[0,1] be the authority of agent i over action class j.

The update equation is

\Lambda_{i,j,t+1}
=
\operatorname{clamp}_{[0,1]}
\left(
\Lambda_{i,j,t}
+ \alpha_j L_t
- \beta_j G_t
- \gamma_j \Lambda_{i,j,t}
\right).

Here L_t is institutional legitimacy, G_t is inequality, and \alpha_j,\beta_j,\gamma_j\ge 0.

F.2 Interior Fixed Point

If the clamp does not bind, the fixed point solves

\Lambda^*
=
\Lambda^* + \alpha_j L - \beta_j G - \gamma_j \Lambda^*.

Rearranging,

\gamma_j \Lambda^*
=
\alpha_j L - \beta_j G,

so

\Lambda^*
=
\frac{\alpha_j L - \beta_j G}{\gamma_j},

provided the right-hand side lies in (0,1).

F.3 Stability

The linearized map around the fixed point has multiplier

1 - \gamma_j.

The fixed point is stable if

|1-\gamma_j| < 1
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
0 < \gamma_j < 2.

If \gamma_j > 1, the trajectory oscillates around the fixed point before settling.

F.4 Robust Authorization

Definition F.1 (Robust Authorization).

\text{authorization}(a) =
\begin{cases}
\text{authorized} & \text{if } \Lambda_{i,j}(t) \ge \tau_j^+,\\[3pt]
\text{uncertainly authorized} & \text{if } \tau_j^- \le \Lambda_{i,j}(t) < \tau_j^+,\\[3pt]
\text{denied} & \text{if } \Lambda_{i,j}(t) < \tau_j^-.
\end{cases}

F.5 Unauthorized Action Probability

If an action is denied or uncertainly authorized, the agent may execute it with probability

\pi_{\text{violate}}(a)
=
\operatorname{clip}_{[0,1]}
\left(
\eta_0
+
\eta_1 \max(0, \tau_j^- - \Lambda_{i,j})
+
\eta_2 (1 - L_t)
\right),

where \eta_0,\eta_1,\eta_2\ge 0.

Every violation is logged in the causal ledger.

F.6 Human Agency Index

Let A_t^{\star} be the set of critical actions executed at time t.

Let A_t^{\text{req}} \subseteq A_t^{\star} be those critical actions for which human authorization was required.

If A_t^{\text{req}}=\varnothing, then H_t = L_t.

Otherwise,

H_t
=
L_t
\cdot
\frac{
\sum_{a\in A_t^{\text{req}}}
w_a
\mathbf{1}[\text{human authorization satisfied for } a]
}{
\sum_{a\in A_t^{\text{req}}} w_a
},

where

w_a
=
1 + \frac{E_{x,\text{required}}(a)}{E_{x,\text{threshold}}}.

The result is clamped to [0,1].

