Appendix I. Hybrid Event Scheduling and Operator-Splitting

I.1 DEVS Formalization

Each continuous buffer k is represented as a DEVS atomic model:

\mathcal{D}_k = (S_k, \delta_{\text{int},k}, \delta_{\text{ext},k}, \lambda_k, ta_k),

where

S_k = \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}

is the buffer level;

\delta_{\text{int},k}(B) = B + \int_0^{ta_k(B)} \left(\dot{B}_k^+ - \dot{B}_k^-\right) ds;

\delta_{\text{ext},k}(B, \Delta B) = \max(0, B + \Delta B);

\lambda_k(B) =
\begin{cases}
\text{failure\_event}_k & \text{if } B \le B_{k,\min},\\
\varnothing & \text{otherwise};
\end{cases}

ta_k(B) =
\min
\left(
\Delta t_{\text{max}},
\inf\{ s>0 : B + \int_0^s (\dot{B}_k^+-\dot{B}_k^-) d\tau \le B_{k,\min} \}
\right).

I.2 Event Detection

The internal transition integrates the ODE until the next threshold crossing. If the crossing occurs between two reporting intervals, the integrator locates the exact crossing time via root-finding.

I.3 Operator-Splitting Order

Within a macro-step, the following order is enforced:

1. Integrate critical buffers with event detection.
2. Process buffer-failure events immediately.
3. Apply discrete action deltas to resources, exergy, waste, knowledge, and authority.
4. Update infrastructure decay and resource depletion.
5. Update population and HANDY-Space using buffer levels from the end of step 1.
6. Update authority and legitimacy using population and inequality from the end of step 5.
7. Record causal ledger and normative audit.

This ordering ensures that a buffer failure detected in step 1 propagates to population in the same macro-step.

