K.2 Transformation Equations

For a transform primitive converting input r_{\text{in}} to output r_{\text{out}} with efficiency \eta_{\text{transform}}\in(0,1):

q_{\text{out}} = \eta_{\text{transform}} q_{\text{in}},

w_{\text{slag}} = (1-\eta_{\text{transform}}) q_{\text{in}}.

Exergy required:

E_{x,\text{required}} = \varepsilon_{\text{transform}} q_{\text{in}},

where \varepsilon_{\text{transform}} is the specific exergy per unit input.

K.3 Knowledge and Information Gain

Let K_t be the knowledge state. The information gain of an observation action is

IG(a^{\text{obs}})
=
H(X_{\text{unknown}} \mid K_t)
-
H(X_{\text{unknown}} \mid K_t, O(a^{\text{obs}})),

where H is entropy and O is the observation function.

In the MVP, X_{\text{unknown}} is the geological composition vector \mathcal{C} of the target region.

The knowledge update is

K_{t+1}
=
K_t
+
\lambda_K K_t
+
\Delta K_o,

where \lambda_K is knowledge decay and \Delta K_o is the knowledge delta from observation.

